  "notes": "USAGE:\nOften used in the form {場馴|ばな}れした (adjective form) or {場馴|ばな}れしている (stative form) to describe someone who appears calm and experienced. Can also be written as {場慣|ばな}れ.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {場馴|ばな}れした{態度|たいど} (an experienced, composed manner)\n- {場馴|ばな}れした{様子|ようす} (an at-ease appearance)\n- すっかり{場馴|ばな}れする (to become completely at ease)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {慣|な}れる: to get used to — general term for becoming accustomed to anything\n- {堂々|どうどう}とする: to be composed — describes confident behavior without implying experience",
